          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`bin_hasRefuelingControl` read back the same way: the displacement block's width."
        },
        "rt_spillTechAdjustment": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`bin_spillTechAdjustment` read back at the rate row, zero off the spillage pollutant-process."
        },
        "rt_refuelingDisplacedVaporRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-2's rate at this row's fuel type."
        },
        "rt_refuelingSpillRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`refuelingFactors.refuelingSpillRate` at this row's fuel type: 0.31 g/gallon on gasoline, diesel and E85 and exactly 0 on CNG and electricity. Diesel HAS a spillage rate and no displacement rate, which is the whole of why the two blocks differ in width."
        },
        "rt_refuelingFuelVolumeDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "MJ/kg",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-7's kJ per gallon at this row's fuel type."
        },
        "rt_hasRefuelingFuelDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Both halves of REFEC-7's inner join at this row's fuel type."
        },
        "rt_spillProgramAdjust": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The county's spillage reduction as the fuel-type fan-out delivers it to this row: the county's value on gasoline and E85, zero on diesel, CNG and electricity."
        },
        "rt_adjustedVaporRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-3/4: `displacedVaporRate (1-P)(1-T) + controlledRefuelingRate (1-P) T`. One convex blend covering an uncontrolled fleet, a fully controlled one and everything between, with no branch."
        },
        "rt_adjustedSpillRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-5/6: `(1 - Pspill)((1 - T) refuelingSpillRate)`."
        },
        "rt_refuelingRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The rate this row is per gallon of: the adjusted vapour rate on a displacement row, the adjusted spillage rate on a spillage row, and zero on every other row in the run."
        },
        "rt_refuelingChainRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "REFEC-8 as a RATIO to the Total Energy Consumption this row chains off: rate over (energy content x fuel density), which is grams of loss per kilojoule burned. `refueling_emission_quantity` is applied at unit energy, because the chain carries the parent's quantity and `lnk_weight` carries the kilojoule-to-MillionBTU rebase that every energy-to-mass edge needs (conventions 77). This is `rt_so2ChainRatio`'s shape exactly: a mass child of energy is a quotient, and the energy is the parent's."
        },
        "rt_hasRefuelingChainRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Is this rate row a refueling row the tables cover? Displacement needs a `refuelingControlTechnology` row and spillage does not; both need a fuel density. The ENERGY-CONTENT half of REFEC-7's inner join is not read here, and that is a stated simplification: it fails for exactly the two fuels whose density is also NULL -- CNG, whose subtype `fuelSubtype` does not carry, and electricity, whose subtype carries NULL -- measured on both databases. The quotient still carries both halves, so a supply with no energy content gives zero rather than a NaN."
        },
        "rt_supplyCarbonContent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`CarbonOxidationByFuelType.sumCarbonContent`: the market-share-weighted carbon content of the row's fuel type's supply."
        },
        "rt_supplyOxidationFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`CarbonOxidationByFuelType.sumOxidationFraction`, weighted the same way. The SQL multiplies the two SUMS, not the sum of their products; with one formulation per fuel type the corpus cannot tell them apart, and this follows the SQL."
        },
        "rt_isCO2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Pollutant 90, atmospheric CO2."
        },
        "rt_isCO2Equivalent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Pollutant 98, CO2 equivalent."
        },
        "rt_isNonHapTog": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Pollutant 88, NonHAPTOG."
        },
        "rt_isNMOG": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Pollutant 80, NMOG: the one positive term of NonHAPTOG."
        },
        "rt_mechanismSelected": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Does the run select, on this row's process, a mechanism the integrated species set belongs to? The switch for all of NonHAPTOG."
        },
        "rt_isIntegratedSpecies": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Is this row's pollutant a member of the integrated species set of a mechanism the run selects on this row's process?"
        },
        "rt_nonHapTogSign": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The row's coefficient in NonHAPTOG: +1 for NMOG, -1 for a member of the set, 0 for everything else. `TOGSpeciationCalculator.sql` spells it the same way, as a signed copy of each input row before one GROUP BY."
        },
        "rt_co2ChainRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J106, CO2AE step 1a: CO2 = energy x carbon content x oxidation fraction x 44/12, the last the mass of a CO2 molecule over that of its carbon. The ratio to energy is everything but the energy; the kilojoules are the edge's (J105). Its presence is the pollutant test alone: `CarbonOxidationByFuelType` has a row for every supplied fuel type, electricity's being zero, so every energy cohort has a CO2 row and electricity's are 0."
        },
        "rt_co2eChainRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J107, CO2AE step 2: the number one on a CO2-equivalent row, as TOG's is. The work is on the three edges, each carrying its input's global warming potential."
        },
        "cty_countyID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "county_rows"
          ],
          "description": "county.countyID. The national table's key; the run selects from it through `rsc_countyID`.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_county",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "countyID"
            }
          }
        },
        "cty_barometricPressure": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "inHg",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "county_rows"
          ],
          "description": "county.barometricPressure, inches of mercury -- 29.095 for Washtenaw. The unit is declared, and every use multiplies by 3.38639 to reach kPa exactly once, in lib/meteorology.esm's `ambient_pressure_kilopascals`.\n\nWHAT IS NOT CARRIED. MOVES runs two `UPDATE County` statements before the humidity pass: MG-1 fills a missing or non-positive pressure from the altitude CLASS, MG-2 then classes a missing altitude from that pressure. Neither is here. MG-1's guard cannot fire -- across all 40 snapshots and 22,815 `County` rows not one has a NULL or non-positive pressure (docs/meteorology-generator.md 8.1) -- and MG-2 writes a column nothing downstream reads. Both arms are checked in components/meteorology.esm against the SQL as ported, which is the only place they can be checked at all.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_county",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "barometricPressure"
            }
          }
        },
        "nha_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "noxhumidityadjust_rows"
          ],
          "description": "noxhumidityadjust.fuelTypeID: 1, 2 and 5. Fuel type 9 is absent, so an electricity rate row takes no humidity correction.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_noxhumidityadjust",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelTypeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "nha_humidityNOxEq": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "noxhumidityadjust_rows"
          ],
          "description": "noxhumidityadjust.humidityNOxEq -- `CFR 86` or `CFR 1065`, decoded to 86 and 1065 by a `codes` map on the binding. An EQUATION carried as data, which is why the two forms are two filtered aggregates below and not one expression with a coefficient switch (conventions 30.4).",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_noxhumidityadjust",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "humidityNOxEq",
              "codes": {
                "map": {
                  "CFR 86": 86,
                  "CFR 1065": 1065
                },
                "case_insensitive": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "nha_humidityTermA": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "noxhumidityadjust_rows"
          ],
          "description": "noxhumidityadjust.humidityTermA: 0.0329 for CFR 86 and 9.953 for CFR 1065. The same column name, two different roles.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_noxhumidityadjust",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "humidityTermA"
            }
          }
        },
        "nha_humidityTermB": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "noxhumidityadjust_rows"
          ],
          "description": "noxhumidityadjust.humidityTermB, 0.832 on the CFR 1065 row and NULL -- hence NaN -- on the two CFR 86 rows. It is read only inside an aggregate whose filter has already excluded those rows, so the NaN never reaches an operator; a document that folded both forms into one expression would return NaN for every gasoline cohort.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_noxhumidityadjust",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "humidityTermB"
            }
          }
        },
        "nha_humidityLowBound": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "noxhumidityadjust_rows"
          ],
          "description": "noxhumidityadjust.humidityLowBound: 3.0 g/kg for CFR 86, 0.002 mole fraction for CFR 1065. Two different UNITS in one column, which is why the bound has to travel with the equation.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_noxhumidityadjust",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "humidityLowBound"
            }
          }
        },
        "nha_humidityUpBound": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "noxhumidityadjust_rows"
          ],
          "description": "noxhumidityadjust.humidityUpBound: 17.71 g/kg for CFR 86, 0.035 mole fraction for CFR 1065.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_noxhumidityadjust",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "humidityUpBound"
            }
          }
        },
        "hd_hourDayID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "hourday_rows"
          ],
          "description": "hourday.hourDayID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_hourday",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "hourDayID"
            }
          }
        },
        "hd_dayID": {
          "type": "parameter",
