          "description": "E1, `least(1, SUM(SHO) / SUM(sourceHours))`. On every run this document has been given it is EXACTLY 1, because A10 made the two sums the same numbers -- so the clamp sits precisely on its boundary, the most fragile place a number can sit, and the soak weight `1 - fractionOfOperating` it feeds is exactly 0. That zero is why `soakActivityFraction` being empty costs these runs nothing, and it is computed rather than assumed: a document that wrote the soak weight as 0 would agree here and be wrong at the first off-network link."
