        },
        "cer_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "crankcaseemissionratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The pollutant of the row's pollutant-process, unpacked."
        },
        "cer_isExhaustSplit": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "crankcaseemissionratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "1 where the row's process is NOT a crankcase process (15, 16, 17). Every such row in the default database is a PM species -- 112, 115, 119 or 120 on running, start, extended idle or APU -- and every one is `SulfatePMCalculator`'s CRANKCASE SPLIT: the share of a species it has already split out of NonECPM that stays in the exhaust process. It is a row filter on a species that exists, not a recipe for making one (conventions 75)."
        },
        "mtr_processID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "methanethcratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "methanethcratio.processID. The methane split is keyed by the PROCESS and not by the pollutant-process, because its input is always THC: there is one row set per process, and the pollutant a rate row carries is what selects the arm (5 methane, 79 NMHC), not what selects the row.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_methanethcratio",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "processID"
            }
          }
        },
        "mtr_fuelSubtypeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "methanethcratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "methanethcratio.fuelSubtypeID. The FUEL SUBTYPE, not the fuel type: gasoline is 10 conventional, 11 reformulated and 12 to 15 the gasohols, and their methane fractions differ. A rate row carries a fuel TYPE, so the subtype is reached through the county's fuel supply and its formulations, market-share weighted, exactly as the criteria ratio reaches them.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_methanethcratio",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "fuelSubtypeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "mtr_regClassID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "methanethcratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "methanethcratio.regClassID. The second width-one trap of this port: source type 21 has exactly one regulatory class, 20, so a document that dropped this key would be right on every run in `runspecs/` and wrong for a light commercial truck. It is carried (conventions §70.3).",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_methanethcratio",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "regClassID"
            }
          }
        },
        "mtr_beginModelYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "methanethcratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "methanethcratio.beginModelYearID, the first model year of the band.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_methanethcratio",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "beginModelYearID"
            }
          }
        },
        "mtr_endModelYearID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "methanethcratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "methanethcratio.endModelYearID, the last.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_methanethcratio",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "endModelYearID"
            }
          }
        },
        "mtr_CH4THCRatio": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "methanethcratio_rows"
          ],
          "description": "methanethcratio.CH4THCRatio, the methane fraction of THC. Methane is THC times it and NMHC is THC times one minus it, so the two species this table produces are complements and the ROW is what both of them need -- absence, not a zero, is what stops them being emitted (§69). It runs 0.0 to 0.959 over the national table's 1,117 rows, which is why the NMHC complement is never zero and can be divided by.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_methanethcratio",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "CH4THCRatio"
            }
          }
        },
