            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S15's temperature adjustment, `general_temp_adjust` (adjust.rs:95-141) in its own branch order. The EV arm was the only one this chain had, because energy and tire wear were the only pollutants it computed; the NOx arm and the fall-through arrive with the criteria pollutants. For total NOx the factor is `(1 + tempAdjust) x k` -- the humidity correction MULTIPLIES the temperature factor rather than adding to it, which is the part a reader would not guess from the table names.\n\nWHAT IS STILL MISSING, AND SAID RATHER THAN LEFT: adjust.rs's FIRST branch is PM (pollutant 112 or 118, process 1 or 2), an exponential in `72 - T` with a ceiling at 72. No RunSpec in this tree emits a PM pollutant, so it is not written here; `fixtures/process-pm-exhaust.esm` carries it and `lib/adjustments.esm` carries its templates. A PM RunSpec would take the fall-through quadratic and be wrong, which is why this is a named gap and not a silence. NOT ON A PERMEATION ROW. `temperatureAdjustment` carries two rows for polProcess 111, and `general_temp_adjust`'s fall-through would read them as a quadratic about 75 degF -- 9.281 at this corpus's 59.5 degF, which is exactly the factor `process-evap-permeation`'s 64 cells came out high by before this arm. Those two rows are PC-2a's, an exponential in the TANK temperature, and `rtDay_permeationTemperatureAdjust` reads them; `EvaporativePermeationCalculator` runs none of S15."
        },
        "rt_batteryEfficiency": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J33: fuelTypeID is FORCED to 9 by setup.rs:3221, so the evefficiency table has no fuel column and the gate is the age GROUP."
        },
        "rt_chargingEfficiency": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The charging half of the divisor, 0.94."
        },
        "rt_hasEvEfficiency": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether evefficiency carries a row for this pollutant-process at all. It does for 9101 and NOT for 11710, and the difference is load-bearing: without this test lib/onroad_activity.esm's `ev_energy_divisor` would divide the tire-wear electricity rate by its own 1e-300 floor and return an infinity."
        },
        "rt_appliesEvDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The divisor applies to an electricity cohort that HAS an evefficiency row -- the LEFT-JOIN reading of adjust.rs:611-616, and the argument `ev_energy_divisor` actually wants."
        },
        "rt_evEnergyDivisor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
