        "pms_fraction": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "pmspeciation_rows"
          ],
          "description": "pmSpeciation.pmSpeciationFraction: 0.7067 of the residue is organic carbon on gasoline, 0.7258 / 0.7417 on diesel either side of 2007.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_pmspeciation",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "pmSpeciationFraction"
            }
          }
        },
        "spmsp_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "THE FOUR SPECIES `SulfatePMCalculator` splits a cohort's PM into: elemental carbon 112, sulfate 115, water 119, and the residue 120 -- which is never emitted and reaches the output three ways, inside NonECPM, inside PM2.5 and speciated into organic carbon."
        },
        "spmsp_parentPollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The RATED block each species is made from: EC is EC, and the other three are NonECPM split three ways."
        },
        "spmsp_isEC": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Selects the species' fraction of its parent: 1 for EC, which is copied."
        },
        "spmsp_isSulfate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Selects the fuel-sulfur-ADJUSTED sulfate fraction."
        },
        "spmsp_isWater": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Selects the adjusted water fraction."
        },
        "spmsp_isResidue": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Selects the residue: 1 minus the UNADJUSTED sulfate and water fractions, times the residue's own base-rate fuel ratio. Unadjusted is not a slip -- it is what the SQL does, and it is what the reference shows: 0.027248 / (0.027248 + 0.92) is the observed 0.028766 sulfate share of gasoline NonECPM in 1980."
        },
        "spmsh_outputPollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmshare_rows"
          ],
          "description": "THE SHARE MATRIX, long format: which species an emitted block is made of. It is the split AND the re-sum at once -- NonECPM is sulfate + water + residue, PM2.5 is all four -- which is why MOVES's chain declaration has a 2-cycle (11801 -> 11501 -> 11801) and this relation does not need one (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 2.8)."
        },
        "spmsh_speciesPollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmshare_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The species this entry takes."
        },
        "spmsh_isSpeciated": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "spmshare_rows"
          ],
          "description": "1 on organic carbon's one entry, whose share of the residue is `pmSpeciation`'s fraction rather than 1."
        },
        "rt_isSPMOutput": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "1 on a rate row whose pollutant `SulfatePMCalculator` produces: 110, 111, 112, 115, 118 or 119. Its quantity is the share matrix times the four species, and not its own rate or a chain. PM10 is not one -- it chains off PM2.5 by `PM10EmissionRatio` as before."
        },
        "rt_hasSulfateFractions": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Does `sulfateFractions` cover this row's process, fuel type, source type and model year? The calculator's inner join: a cohort without one emits no PM species at all."
        },
        "rt_spmSulfateFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`SulfateFraction = Sum marketShare x SulfatenonECPMFraction x (1 + BaseFuelSulfateFraction x (sulfurLevel / BaseFuelSulfurLevel - 1))` over the county's formulations of this row's fuel type: 0.027248 on 1980 gasoline, 0.066530 on 2020, 0.014773 on 1980 diesel."
        },
        "rt_spmWaterFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The same adjustment on the water fraction."
        },
        "rt_spmResidueFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`1 - SulfatenonECPMFraction - H2OnonECPMFraction`, UNADJUSTED -- see `spmsp_isResidue`."
        },
        "rt_residuePolProcessID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The residue's own pollutant-process at this row's process, 12001 on running exhaust: the key its base-rate fuel ratio is stored under."
        },
        "rt_residueFuelRatioExact": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The residue's `generalFuelRatio`, where a row covers."
        },
        "rt_hasResidueFuelRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Does one?"
        },
        "rt_residueFuelRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The residue's base-rate fuel ratio, 1 where no row covers -- the same strings as EC's, so 1.0909107 on gasoline and E85 from 2001 and 0.9727 on diesel through 2006."
        },
        "rt_spmSpeciesFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "spmspecies_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How much of its parent each species is: 1 for EC, the adjusted sulfate and water fractions, and the residue fraction times the residue's fuel ratio."
        },
        "rt_spmSplitRatio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The crankcase split: the share of each species that stays in THIS row's process, from `crankcaseEmissionRatio` at the species' own pollutant -- the exhaust-process rows conventions 75 says are this calculator's. 1.0 on every running-exhaust row of the default database; carried because it is the arithmetic, and it is where a start- or crankcase-process PM run would differ."
        },
        "rt_pmSpeciationFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`pmSpeciation`'s fraction of the residue that is this row's pollutant -- organic carbon's, on the 11101 rows."
        },
        "rt_spmShare": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "spmspecies_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How much of each species this rate row emits: the share matrix at the row's pollutant, with organic carbon's entry replaced by its speciation fraction."
        },
        "rtDay_spmParent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "spmspecies_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Each species' parent quantity: the RATED quantity of the EC or NonECPM row of the same source bin and process. A self-join of the rate relation, the one `rtDay_quantChained` uses."
        },
        "rtDay_spmSpecies": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "spmspecies_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The four species of this row's cohort, in the output's units."
        },
        "rtDay_spmQuant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The share matrix times the species: this row's quantity when it is one of `SulfatePMCalculator`'s blocks."
        },
        "rt_spmParentSurvives": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Does a rated parent of some species this row takes survive in the same source bin?"
        },
        "rt_spmSurvives": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "A `SulfatePMCalculator` block's own survival: covered by `sulfateFractions` AND made of a surviving parent. Organic carbon and water have no `pollutantProcessModelYear` row and so are never SELECTED -- they exist only because this calculator writes them."
        },
        "rtDay_quantRated": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S17 and S18: rate x activity, in the output's own units -- what `rtDay_quantDirect` was before `SulfatePMCalculator` took over six blocks. Exactly zero on a chained pollutant-process."
        },
        "rtDay_quantDirect": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The row's OWN quantity, before any chain: `rtDay_quantRated` everywhere except on `SulfatePMCalculator`'s six blocks, where it is the share matrix times the four species. Putting it HERE, and not in the output, is what lets PM10 chain off PM2.5 exactly as it chained off nothing before."
        },
        "rtDay_chainGen1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The chain term computed against the parent's OWN-RATE quantity: correct for a species whose parent carries a rate, which is every chain one deep. One rung of the chain's value fixed point -- see lib/chaining.esm for why the chain is a fixed point and why three rungs is the measured maximum, and `run_chainDepthExceeded` for the per-run assertion that this run does not need a fourth."
        },
        "rtDay_quantGen1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The quantity after one rung: own rate plus a parent's own rate scaled. Zero on a species two rungs from a rate, which is what the next generation repairs. One rung of the chain's value fixed point -- see lib/chaining.esm for why the chain is a fixed point and why three rungs is the measured maximum, and `run_chainDepthExceeded` for the per-run assertion that this run does not need a fourth."
        },
        "rtDay_chainGen2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The chain term computed against the parent's quantity after one rung. One rung of the chain's value fixed point -- see lib/chaining.esm for why the chain is a fixed point and why three rungs is the measured maximum, and `run_chainDepthExceeded` for the per-run assertion that this run does not need a fourth."
        },
        "rtDay_quantGen2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The quantity after two rungs. One rung of the chain's value fixed point -- see lib/chaining.esm for why the chain is a fixed point and why three rungs is the measured maximum, and `run_chainDepthExceeded` for the per-run assertion that this run does not need a fourth."
        },
        "rtDay_quantChained": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The chain term at the THIRD and last rung: the parent's quantity after two rungs, at the same source bin and day, times this row's ratio. It is a SELF-JOIN of the rate relation -- the chained row and the row it is chained from are two rows of one relation -- so the clause names its two sides with `syms` (CONFORMANCE_SPEC 5.5.8). On an unchained row the ratio is 0 and the chain key is 0, which matches no pollutant-process, so both halves say the same thing. PM10BrakeTireCalculator's whole arithmetic is the one-rung case of this. Per county. One rung of the chain's value fixed point -- see lib/chaining.esm for why the chain is a fixed point and why three rungs is the measured maximum, and `run_chainDepthExceeded` for the per-run assertion that this run does not need a fourth."
        },
        "rtDay_nonHapTogSum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J108, TOGSpeciationCalculator: NMOG minus the integrated species, on this 88 row's source bin, process and day, before the clamp. It reads each input's FINISHED quantity, rate path plus chain, because NonHAPTOG is four rungs from THC -- THC, NMHC, VOC, a toxic -- one more than the chain unrolls, and a leaf: nothing is chained from it, so it can be computed after the chain rather than as a fourth rung of it."
        },
        "rtDay_nonHapTog": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "NonHAPTOG, clamped at zero. The SQL clamps each worker-output cell, which is finer than a cohort and coarser than a source bin; this clamps the source bin. The two agree unless a bin's NMOG is below its own toxics, and in this corpus the smallest unclamped cell is 0.0015 g -- so the corpus cannot tell them apart, and the bin is the only grain this relation has."
        },
        "rtDay_quant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The emitted quantity: its own rate path plus its chain. Every rate row is exactly one of the two, so the sum is a union and not a double count -- `run_chainedRowCount` is the test. Per county, which is the axis the output relation's second level reads it at. Plus NonHAPTOG, which is neither and is zero off pollutant 88."
        },
        "rt_parentEmitsGen4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Generation 4, which exists only to be compared with generation 3: does the parent emit after three rungs? A presence pass carries no day, county or month, so a fourth costs one more self-join of the rate relation and nothing else."
        },
        "rt_emitsGen4": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "`rt_emits` after four rungs. Equal to `rt_emits` on every RunSpec in `runspecs/`, and that equality is the whole point: it is what turns \"three rungs is enough\" from an assumption into a measurement the run itself makes."
        },
        "run_chainDepthExceeded": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many rate rows a FOURTH rung of the chain would newly emit: 0, asserted. lib/chaining.esm records that three is the longest chain in the whole snapshot corpus; this is the run's own check of it, and a run that broke it would leave its deepest species at zero rather than wrong -- which this counts and the shape checker would then see as missing rows."
        },
        "run_oxySpeciationReached": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many `HCSpeciation` rows with a non-zero `oxySpeciation` this run's joins reach: 0, asserted. The oxygenate term is the one part of `speciation_factor` this document does not carry, and this is what says the omission is a reading of the DATA rather than of MOVES."
        },
        "run_chainedRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many selected rate rows carry a chain ratio. It reads the PRESENCE flag and not `rt_chainRatio > 0`, for the reason §70.2 gives: `CrankcaseEmissionRatio` carries ratios of exactly zero and those cohorts are emitted. A rate row can never have both a ratio and a rate of its own, which is what makes `rtDay_quant`'s sum a union."
        },
        "bin_isSelectedAt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The bin's membership read back at the rate row, so the chained block's row count can be counted without a second rank."
        },
        "pcoh_ordinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Its own position, 1..n_runspecpollutantprocess x n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype. This relation is the pollutant-process crossed with the COHORT candidate grid -- the rate relation with the source bin divided out -- and it exists because the output relation is keyed by (block, cohort) and the rate relation is keyed by (block, BIN). J78."
        },
        "pcoh_polProcOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which pollutant-process this (block, cohort) pair is for. Pollutant-process major, the same order `rate_rows` uses, which is what makes the rank below agree with the emitted row order."
        },
        "pcoh_cohortOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "And which cohort candidate, 1..n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype."
        },
        "pcoh_outputBlockOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output block this pair's pollutant-process owns, read back from `rspp_outputOrdinal`. 0 on every pair of a pollutant-process that is not emitted."
        },
        "pcoh_hasEmittingRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Does ANY rate row of this (pollutant-process, cohort) pair put a number in MOVESOutput? The OR over the cohort's source bins of `rt_emits`. It is NOT the same question as whether the pair is emitted: six of `expand-criteria`'s eight selected pollutant-processes have rate rows that emit and only three of them happen on a road, so this counts 744 pairs where the run emits 372. On a retagging pollutant-process it asks of the modes the block keeps (`rt_ownBlockEmits`)."
        },
        "pcoh_emits": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "And is its pollutant-process an emitted BLOCK? A pair emits when a rate row of it emits AND the road-type test kept its block -- the two conditions the old `(block - 1) x n_outputCohort + cohortRank` packing carried in its `and`, which is why they have to be spelled again here."
        },
        "pcoh_prefixEmits": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "An inclusive prefix count of `rc_emits` over the whole pollutant-process-major relation (docs/esm-conventions.md §22)."
        },
        "pcoh_rateOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The prefix count ZEROED on the pairs that do not emit, so every emitted (block, cohort) pair has a dense 1..n_outputRate and every other pair has 0. This is the output relation's leading key and it replaces the (block - 1) x n_outputCohort + cohortRank packing, which could only number a rectangle."
        },
        "pcoh_cohortRank": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "ratecohort_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The cohort's GLOBAL dense rank, 1..cohortSurvivorCount, which `coh_rank` is the other side of. The output row reads its model year, fuel type and source type from the cohort relation through this, not through the rate ordinal, because a key column is read from the relation that OWNS it."
        },
        "rateSurvivorCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs emit, computed from the chain, so `n_outputRate` is a CHECKED declaration rather than a transcription. It equals `outputPolProcessCount` x `cohortSurvivorCount` exactly when the run is a rectangle, and is LESS when a chained block is narrower than its parent; run-tests.sh prints which. It counts the process-93 pairs a retagging pollutant-process adds (`spc_emits`) as well."
        },
        "rt_outputOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "rate_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Where this rate row lands in the output relation: the dense rank of its (pollutant-process, cohort) PAIR, read from `rc_rateOrdinal`, and 0 when that pair does not emit. Every source bin of the same cohort carries the same ordinal and `out_emissionQuant` sums over them, which is what it did before; what changed at J78 is that the number is a rank and no longer (block - 1) x n_outputCohort + rank, an arithmetic that assumed every block is the same width."
        },
        "outPolProcOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which output block this row belongs to, read BACK from the pair relation through the rate rank. It used to be a division of the row index by a fixed block length; a block length is exactly what a ragged output does not have (J78)."
        },
        "outRateOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S17's row structure: the output relation is (pollutant-process, cohort) PAIR major, then county, then month, then day type. This is the pair's dense rank, 1..n_outputRate, and `rc_rateOrdinal` is the other side of it. The county, month and day levels moved INSIDE the pair at J78; nothing reads the emitted order but `process-tirewear`'s byte-for-byte check, whose run has one county, one month and one day type, so its rows are where they were."
        },
        "outRateOffset": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The row's offset within its pair's block of counties x months x day types, which the three levels below decompose in that order."
        },
        "outCountyOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Which of the run's counties this output row is for. The output relation is pollutant-process major, then COUNTY, then day type, then cohort; `expand-counties` is the run that makes this level wider than one."
        },
        "outCountyOffset": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The position of this row within its county's block, which is what the day and cohort levels decompose."
        },
        "outMonthOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Month-major within the county's block."
        },
        "outDayOrdinal": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Day-major within the county's block."
        },
        "outCohortRank": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The surviving cohort's GLOBAL rank, 1..cohortSurvivorCount, which `coh_rank` is the other side of. It is read back from the pair relation rather than decomposed out of the row index, because the pair's position in its block is not the cohort's rank once a block is narrower than the widest one."
        },
        "out_modelYearID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The output row's model year, read BACK through the rank join. A KEY column is read from the relation that OWNS it -- this one from the cohort relation through the rank, not from the rate relation through `rt_outputOrdinal` -- because since 7e several rate rows can share an output row and a `sum_product` over them would add their keys together. The VALUE columns below keep the rate join, where that sum is the point."
        },
        "out_fuelTypeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Its fuel type. A KEY column is read from the relation that OWNS it -- this one from the cohort relation through the rank, not from the rate relation through `rt_outputOrdinal` -- because since 7e several rate rows can share an output row and a `sum_product` over them would add their keys together. The VALUE columns below keep the rate join, where that sum is the point."
        },
        "out_pollutantID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Its pollutant: 91, 107 or 117. A KEY column is read from the relation that OWNS it -- this one from the cohort relation through the rank, not from the rate relation through `rt_outputOrdinal` -- because since 7e several rate rows can share an output row and a `sum_product` over them would add their keys together. The VALUE columns below keep the rate join, where that sum is the point."
        },
        "out_processID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Its process: 1 or 9. A KEY column is read from the relation that OWNS it -- this one from the cohort relation through the rank, not from the rate relation through `rt_outputOrdinal` -- because since 7e several rate rows can share an output row and a `sum_product` over them would add their keys together. The VALUE columns below keep the rate join, where that sum is the point. On a shore-power row it is 93, which the calculator wrote and the RunSpec never selected."
        },
        "out_meanBaseRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The collapsed base rate on the output row. Emitted as an extra column: the comparator ignores columns MOVESOutput does not have, and having it in the CSV is what makes a disagreement attributable to the rate or to the activity."
        },
        "out_adjustedMeanBaseRate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The same after S15."
        },
        "out_emissionQuantDirect": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The row's own rate path, before the chain -- 0 on every PM10 row."
        },
        "out_emissionQuant": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "output_rows"
          ],
          "description": "S18: Million BTU for pollutant 91 and grams for 107 and 117. THE compared column."
        },
        "lnk_linkLength": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "link_rows"
          ],
          "description": "link.linkLength, miles. A PROJECT link's length; NULL on every default-database link, which is read only behind `run_isProjectDomain`.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_link",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "linkLength"
            }
          }
        },
        "lnk_linkVolume": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "link_rows"
          ],
          "description": "link.linkVolume, vehicles per hour. A PROJECT link's traffic volume, the root of `ProjectTAG`'s SHO; NULL on every default-database link.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_link",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "linkVolume"
            }
          }
        },
        "lnk_linkAvgSpeed": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "link_rows"
          ],
          "description": "link.linkAvgSpeed, mph. A PROJECT link's average speed: it brackets the link between two drive schedules and divides its length into hours. NULL on every default-database link.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_link",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "linkAvgSpeed"
            }
          }
        },
        "lnk_linkAvgGrade": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "percent",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "link_rows"
          ],
          "description": "link.linkAvgGrade, per cent. A PROJECT link's grade, copied onto every second of both bracketing schedules. NULL on every default-database link.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_link",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "linkAvgGrade"
            }
          }
        },
        "lsth_linkID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "linksourcetypehour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "linkSourceTypeHour.linkID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_linksourcetypehour",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "linkID"
            }
          }
        },
        "lsth_sourceTypeID": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "linksourcetypehour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "linkSourceTypeHour.sourceTypeID.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_linksourcetypehour",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "sourceTypeID"
            }
          }
        },
        "lsth_sourceTypeHourFraction": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "linksourcetypehour_rows"
          ],
          "description": "linkSourceTypeHour.sourceTypeHourFraction: the share of a project link's volume that is this source type. Despite the name it carries no hour.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_linksourcetypehour",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "sourceTypeHourFraction"
            }
          }
        },
        "rsdom_modelDomain": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "shape": [
            "runspecdomain_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The RunSpec's `<modeldomain value>`, decoded by a `codes` map onto the `model_domain` enum. NATIONAL is ModelDomain.java's deprecated spelling of DEFAULT and decodes the same.",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "db_runspecdomain",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "modelDomain",
              "codes": {
                "map": {
                  "DEFAULT": 1,
                  "NATIONAL": 1,
                  "SINGLE": 2,
                  "PROJECT": 3
                },
                "case_insensitive": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "run_isProjectDomain": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "1 when the RunSpec's domain is PROJECT. It is the one switch the domain throws in this model, and it throws three things: SHO is ProjectTAG's link-volume product rather than TotalActivityGenerator's VMT allocation (`act_sho`), a running-exhaust pollutant-process weights its operating modes by the LINK's distribution rather than the average-speed bins' (`pp_W`), and MOVESOutput carries zone and link (`out_zoneID`, `out_linkID`). Which LINK table the run reads is not switched here: the domain document declares it (moves-onroad.esm and inputs/)."
        },
        "run_domainRowCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Rows in runspecdomain. Exactly 1, asserted through `run_domainUnported`: a sum over two domain rows would be a domain no RunSpec has."
        },
        "run_linkLength": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The selected link's linkLength in each county -- selected the way `run_linkID` is -- and 0 outside PROJECT domain, where the default database's link carries NULL here and nothing reads it."
        },
        "run_linkVolume": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The selected link's linkVolume in each county -- selected the way `run_linkID` is -- and 0 outside PROJECT domain, where the default database's link carries NULL here and nothing reads it."
        },
        "run_linkAvgSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The selected link's linkAvgSpeed in each county -- selected the way `run_linkID` is -- and 0 outside PROJECT domain, where the default database's link carries NULL here and nothing reads it."
        },
        "run_linkAvgGrade": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The selected link's linkAvgGrade in each county -- selected the way `run_linkID` is -- and 0 outside PROJECT domain, where the default database's link carries NULL here and nothing reads it."
        },
        "run_linkCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspeccounty_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many links the county/road-type join selects in each county. 1 on every run here. The four `run_link*` columns are SUMS over this join, right while it selects one row; a project of two links on one road type would add their ids, so `run_domainUnported` counts a county where it is not 1."
        },
        "run_projectLinkSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The project link's average speed, summed over the run's one county."
        },
        "run_projectLinkGrade": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The project link's grade, summed over the run's one county."
        },
        "act_projectSho": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "activity_rows",
            "runspeccounty_rows",
            "runspecsourcetype_rows",
            "runspecmonth_rows"
          ],
          "description": "ProjectTAG.allocateTotalActivityBasis's SHO (ProjectTAG.java:354-385): linkVolume x sourceTypeHourFraction x noOfRealDays x ageFraction x least(linkLength/linkAvgSpeed, 1), in the SQL's association. It reads no VMT, no road-type distribution and no SHO allocation factor -- a project's activity is its links' volumes -- and the month is a label it carries rather than a factor. 0 in a DEFAULT-domain run, whose linkSourceTypeHour is empty."
        },
        "lomd_gradeAcceleration": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "mi/(h*s)",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "9.81/0.44704 x sin(atan(grade/100)): the acceleration-equivalent of the project link's grade, added to every one of the three accelerations the braking test reads (LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator.java:1006-1009). 0 at grade 0, which is the corpus's only grade."
        },
        "lomd_at0": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "mi/(h*s)",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows"
          ],
          "description": "At0 = coalesce((speed[t] - speed[t-1]) + grade, 0.0), java:1006. A BACKWARD difference only: a schedule's first second has no predecessor and gets 0, where `dss_acceleration` copies its successor's -- the Java's @algorithm comment claims the forward fallback and its SQL does not have it (docs/link-operating-mode-distribution.md 2.3)."
        },
        "lomd_at1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "mi/(h*s)",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows"
          ],
          "description": "At1 = coalesce((speed[t-1] - speed[t-2]) + grade, 0.0): NULL, and so 0, unless both seconds exist."
        },
        "lomd_at2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "mi/(h*s)",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows"
          ],
          "description": "At2 = coalesce((speed[t-2] - speed[t-3]) + grade, 0.0)."
        },
        "lomd_isBraking": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows"
          ],
          "description": "At0 <= -2 or (At0 < -1 and At1 < -1 and At2 < -1), the CASE's third arm. The thresholds are READ from operatingMode's Braking row, as `dss_isBraking` reads them; the SQL writes the same -2 and -1 as literals. Unlike the base-rate path there is no presence requirement: a missing neighbour is a 0 acceleration, which is not below -1."
        },
        "lomd_accelerationMs": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s^2",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows"
          ],
          "description": "coalesce(speed[t] - speed[t-1], 0.0) x 0.44704, the acceleration term of the link generator's VSP: the converted DIFFERENCE, with no grade and no forward fallback."
        },
        "lomd_vsp": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kW/tonne",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "java:1010-1015: the road-load polynomial `vehicle_specific_power` carries, with the link's acceleration, plus `grade_specific_power` for the grade. lib/drive_cycle.esm measures why one polynomial serves both generators."
        },
        "lomd_binnedModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "buildOpModeClause's rectangles (java:241-300) as a sum: opModeID 1..99 less 26 and 36 is `om_isBinnedRunningMode`'s set plus mode 1, whose -1 <= speed < 1 rectangle the idle arm has always claimed first, so the two sets assign the same mode to every second."
        },
        "lomd_binnedModeMatches": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The same sum without the id: 1 on a second some rectangle admits, 0 on one the SQL's CASE sends to -1, which is still counted in the schedule's total."
        },
        "lomd_isStopped": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows"
          ],
          "description": "speed = 0, the CASE's first arm, mode 501. It folds into mode 1 for every pollutant-process but brake-wear PM, AFTER each was divided by the schedule's total and rounded -- so its seconds are counted apart from the idle ones, and the two five-decimal quotients are added."
        },
        "lomd_opModeID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The second's mode in the CASE's order: stopped or idle (speed < 1), then braking, then the rectangles."
        },
        "lomd_hasOpMode": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_second_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether any arm of the CASE but the -1 fallback took the second."
        },
        "lomd_totalSeconds": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_schedule_assoc_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "secondTotal = count(*) over the schedule (java:1060): EVERY second, the first and the unassigned ones included -- where `dsa_totalSeconds` counts only seconds after 0 that took a mode."
        },
        "lomd_stoppedSeconds": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_schedule_assoc_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Seconds of the schedule at speed 0, mode 501."
        },
        "lomd_modeSeconds": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_schedule_assoc_rows",
            "operating_mode_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "secondCount per mode, the stopped seconds left out (they are mode 501, not mode 1, until after the quotient)."
        },
        "lomd_modeFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "drive_schedule_assoc_rows",
            "operating_mode_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "secondCount * 1.0 / secondTotal, a DECIMAL rounded half-up at FIVE places (lib/operating_mode.esm's `link_op_mode_fraction`; docs/link-operating-mode-distribution.md 2.4), with mode 501's own quotient added to mode 1's -- the `group by ... sum(opModeFraction)` of the fold. MOVES then stores it in a FLOAT column, which this does not model: binary32 moves a fraction by at most 6e-8 of itself, and the run's cells are compared at 2e-5."
        },
        "lomd_hasAtOrBelow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the source type has a candidate schedule for the greatest averageSpeed AT OR BELOW the link's: the low bracket."
        },
        "lomd_atOrBelowSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The greatest averageSpeed AT OR BELOW the link's: the low bracket."
        },
        "lomd_hasAbove": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the source type has a candidate schedule for the least averageSpeed strictly ABOVE the link's: the low bracket's out-of-bounds fallback."
        },
        "lomd_aboveSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The least averageSpeed strictly ABOVE the link's: the low bracket's out-of-bounds fallback."
        },
        "lomd_hasAtOrAbove": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the source type has a candidate schedule for the least averageSpeed AT OR ABOVE the link's: the high bracket."
        },
        "lomd_atOrAboveSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The least averageSpeed AT OR ABOVE the link's: the high bracket."
        },
        "lomd_hasBelow": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether the source type has a candidate schedule for the greatest averageSpeed strictly BELOW the link's: the high bracket's out-of-bounds fallback."
        },
        "lomd_belowSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The greatest averageSpeed strictly BELOW the link's: the high bracket's out-of-bounds fallback."
        },
        "lomd_lowSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The low bracket's speed: at or below the link's if any schedule is, else the fallback."
        },
        "lomd_highSpeed": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The high bracket's speed: the same precedence, mirrored -- at or above the link's if any schedule is, else the fastest below it."
        },
        "lomd_outOfBoundsCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "isOutOfBoundsLow + isOutOfBoundsHigh. Either one is a MOVES terminal error unless ALLOW_DRIVE_CYCLE_EXTRAPOLATION, so a run that reaches one is not a run this model reproduces; `run_domainUnported` counts it."
        },
        "lomd_lowScheduleID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The low bracket's schedule: max(driveScheduleID) among the candidates at its speed, which is how the SQL breaks a tie."
        },
        "lomd_highScheduleID": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The high bracket's schedule: max(driveScheduleID) among the candidates at its speed, which is how the SQL breaks a tie."
        },
        "lomd_factor": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecsourcetype_rows"
          ],
          "description": "(linkAvgSpeed - low) / (high - low), and 0 when one schedule brackets both sides (java:690)."
        },
        "lomd_lowFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "operating_mode_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The low bracket's distribution, per vehicle."
        },
        "lomd_highFraction": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "operating_mode_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The high bracket's distribution, per vehicle."
        },
        "lomd_W": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "operating_mode_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "low + (high - low) x factor over EVERY mode, a mode one bracket never entered reading 0, and the non-positive ones dropped (java:700-720) -- the project link's operating-mode distribution, at the BASE mode: `SourceTypePhysics` lifts it to opModeID + 1000 and lifts the same vehicles' emission rates with it, and the chain here keys both on the base mode and the physics row, as it does at every other scale."
        },
        "rspp_usesLinkModes": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Whether a PROJECT run weights this pollutant-process by the link's operating-mode distribution: Running Exhaust. Brake wear reads it too in MOVES, keeping mode 501 for its PM, and that arm is not ported -- `run_domainUnported` counts an emitted pollutant-process this leaves out."
        },
        "pp_WSpeedBins": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "runspecpollutantprocess_rows",
            "runspecday_rows",
            "operating_mode_rows",
            "physicsrow_rows"
          ],
          "description": "W, and IT IS KEYED BY THE POLLUTANT-PROCESS HERE -- the one structural difference between this fixture and `process-brakewear`. `BaseRateGenerator` is invoked per process and `RatesOpModeDistribution` is written by two different generators: for Running Exhaust and Brakewear it drives the drive cycles itself (mod.rs:156-161, `should_process_drive_cycles = process_id == 1 || process_id == 9`), and for Tirewear it reads what `AverageSpeedOperatingModeDistributionGenerator` wrote (avg_speed_op_mode_distribution.rs:110-116, `TIREWEAR_PROCESS = ProcessId(10)`). Both give the same shape -- Sum over the speed bins of avgSpeedFraction x opModeFraction, aggregate.rs:365-417 -- and differ only in which mode fraction they carry, so this is ONE aggregate with the mode fraction selected per pollutant-process rather than two relations and a branch downstream."
        },
        "run_domainUnported": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "How many things this run asks of its DOMAIN that the model does not do: 0, asserted by tools/check-runspec-shape.py, and the licence for every PROJECT-domain number. It counts a runspecdomain that is not one row; in PROJECT domain, a county whose join selects other than one link, a second county, an emitted pollutant-process other than running exhaust (brake wear's mode-501 arm, tire wear's and the evaporative and start processes' project generators are not ported), and a bracketing schedule out of bounds (a MOVES terminal error); and outside it, any linkSourceTypeHour row, which only ProjectTAG reads. None of those fail loudly on their own -- each would emit a plausible wrong number -- which is why they are counted rather than trusted. Since the SINGLE-county runs it also counts a ZoneRoadType input row whose key the default lacks (a row the merge would ADD, which relations on the default side's axis cannot see), and a hotellingHourFraction, hotellingAgeFraction or hotellingMonthAdjust row at a run's zone when it selects a hotelling process -- AdjustHotelling's three other adjustments are not ported. And a Zone input row whose zone the default lacks."
        },
        "run_projectShortfall": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "The PROJECT-domain half of `run_domainUnported`."
        },
        "run_linkCountMismatches": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Counties whose county/road-type join selects other than exactly one link."
        },
        "run_countyCount": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Counties the run selects."
        },
        "run_unportedProjectProcesses": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "run_rows"
          ],
          "description": "Emitted pollutant-processes whose PROJECT-domain operating modes this model does not compute."
        },
