        {
          "_comment": "A row emits if the rate table covers it, or if a CHAIN does. The second arm is `run_chainedRowCount`'s own spelling -- a chain ratio at a selected source bin -- and it cannot be written as `rt_survives` with something added, because `rt_isSelected` is 0 on every rate row of a chained pollutant-process: 10710 has no `pollutantprocessmodelyear` row, which is exactly what makes it chained. `process-tirewear` emits three blocks and two of them carry a rate.",
          "lhs": "rt_emitsChained",
